WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.317
Run this example to compare several functions at once.

00:00:03.317 --> 00:00:06.382
UPPER and LOWER change letter case.

00:00:06.382 --> 00:00:09.707
BTRIM removes spaces from the beginning and end.

00:00:09.707 --> 00:00:13.627
INITCAP creates a display-style name after trimming.

00:00:13.627 --> 00:00:21.472
LENGTH shows why invisible spaces matter: raw and trimmed strings can have different lengths even when they

00:00:21.472 --> 00:00:26.342
look similar on screen. Text cleaning should separate normalization from interpretation.

00:00:26.342 --> 00:00:31.812
Trimming spaces or standardizing case is usually safe when the rule is documented;

00:00:31.812 --> 00:00:37.612
correcting a person's name or guessing an email address is a much stronger intervention.

00:00:37.612 --> 00:00:41.141
Preserve the original value when auditability matters.
